[codex] name: planning-with-files
[codex] description: Use this by default for non-trivial multi-step work that needs persistent planning, progress tracking, or durable notes on disk. Trigger when a task will likely span multiple tool calls, research steps, verification loops, or enough context that the plan should not live only in transient chat memory.
[codex] version: 0.1.0
[codex] ---
[codex] 
[codex] # Planning with Files
[codex] 
[codex] Work like Manus: use persistent markdown files as your working memory on disk.
[codex] 
[codex] This is not just an optional planning style. It should be the default persistence layer for complex Codex work.
[codex] 
[codex] Use it proactively when:
[codex] 
[codex] - the task will likely take more than a few tool calls
[codex] - progress needs to be tracked across phases
[codex] - findings or evidence must be preserved while working
[codex] - the task may branch, pause, or resume later
[codex] - relying on chat context alone would be fragile
[codex] 
[codex] ## Quick Start
[codex] 
[codex] Before ANY complex task:
[codex] 
[codex] 1. **Create `task_plan.md`** in the working directory
[codex] 2. **Define phases** with checkboxes
[codex] 3. **Update after each phase** - mark [x] and change status
[codex] 4. **Read before deciding** - refresh goals in attention window
[codex] 
[codex] ## The 3-File Pattern
[codex] 
[codex] For every non-trivial task, create THREE files:
[codex] 
[codex] | File | Purpose | When to Update |
[codex] |------|---------|----------------|
[codex] | `task_plan.md` | Track phases and progress | After each phase |
[codex] | `notes.md` | Store findings and research | During research |
[codex] | `[deliverable].md` | Final output | At completion |
[codex] 
[codex] ## Core Workflow
[codex] 
[codex] ```
[codex] Loop 1: Create task_plan.md with goal and phases
[codex] Loop 2: Research → save to notes.md → update task_plan.md
[codex] Loop 3: Read notes.md → create deliverable → update task_plan.md
[codex] Loop 4: Deliver final output
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] ### The Loop in Detail
[codex] 
[codex] **Before each major action:**
[codex] ```bash
[codex] Read task_plan.md  # Refresh goals in attention window
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] **After each phase:**
[codex] ```bash
[codex] Edit task_plan.md  # Mark [x], update status
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] **When storing information:**
[codex] ```bash
[codex] Write notes.md     # Don't stuff context, store in file
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] ## task_plan.md Template
[codex] 
[codex] Create this file FIRST for any complex task:
[codex] 
[codex] ```markdown
[codex] # Task Plan: [Brief Description]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Goal
[codex] [One sentence describing the end state]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Phases
[codex] - [ ] Phase 1: Plan and setup
[codex] - [ ] Phase 2: Research/gather information
[codex] - [ ] Phase 3: Execute/build
[codex] - [ ] Phase 4: Review and deliver
[codex] 
[codex] ## Key Questions
[codex] 1. [Question to answer]
[codex] 2. [Question to answer]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Decisions Made
[codex] - [Decision]: [Rationale]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Errors Encountered
[codex] - [Error]: [Resolution]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Status
[codex] **Currently in Phase X** - [What I'm doing now]
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] ## notes.md Template
[codex] 
[codex] For research and findings:
[codex] 
[codex] ```markdown
[codex] # Notes: [Topic]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Sources
[codex] 
[codex] ### Source 1: [Name]
[codex] - URL: [link]
[codex] - Key points:
[codex]   - [Finding]
[codex]   - [Finding]
[codex] 
[codex] ## Synthesized Findings
[codex] 
[codex] ### [Category]
[codex] - [Finding]
[codex] - [Finding]
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] ## Critical Rules
[codex] 
[codex] ### 1. ALWAYS Create Plan First
[codex] Never start a complex task without `task_plan.md`. This is non-negotiable.
[codex] 
[codex] ### 2. Read Before Decide
[codex] Before any major decision, read the plan file. This keeps goals in your attention window.
[codex] 
[codex] ### 3. Update After Act
[codex] After completing any phase, immediately update the plan file:
[codex] - Mark completed phases with [x]
[codex] - Update the Status section
[codex] - Log any errors encountered
[codex] 
[codex] ### 4. Store, Don't Stuff
[codex] Large outputs go to files, not context. Keep only paths in working memory.
[codex] 
[codex] ### 5. Log All Errors
[codex] Every error goes in the "Errors Encountered" section. This builds knowledge for future tasks.
[codex] 
[codex] ## When to Use This Pattern
[codex] 
[codex] **Use 3-file pattern for:**
[codex] - Multi-step tasks (3+ steps)
[codex] - Research tasks
[codex] - Building/creating something
[codex] - Tasks spanning multiple tool calls
[codex] - Anything requiring organization
[codex] 
[codex] **Skip for:**
[codex] - Simple questions
[codex] - Single-file edits
[codex] - Quick lookups
[codex] 
[codex] ## Anti-Patterns to Avoid
[codex] 
[codex] | Don't | Do Instead |
[codex] |-------|------------|
[codex] | Use TodoWrite for persistence | Create `task_plan.md` file |
[codex] | State goals once and forget | Re-read plan before each decision |
[codex] | Hide errors and retry | Log errors to plan file |
[codex] | Stuff everything in context | Store large content in files |
[codex] | Start executing immediately | Create plan file FIRST |
[codex] 
[codex] ## Advanced Patterns
[codex] 
[codex] See [reference.md](reference.md) for:
[codex] - Attention manipulation techniques
[codex] - Error recovery patterns
[codex] - Context optimization from Manus
[codex] 
[codex] See [examples.md](examples.md) for:
[codex] - Real task examples
[codex] - Complex workflow patterns
[codex] 
