[codex] 
[codex] # Daily Coding Checklist
[codex] 
[codex] A minimal coding quality assurance checklist ensuring every code modification follows best practices.
[codex] 
[codex] ## When to Use
[codex] 
[codex] Use this skill for:
[codex] - Implementing new features
[codex] - Adding code or modifying existing code
[codex] - User requests like "write a...", "implement...", "add...", or "modify..."
[codex] - Any coding task that involves Edit or Write tools
[codex] 
[codex] ## When Not to Use
[codex] 
[codex] Do not use this skill for:
[codex] - Pure reading or understanding tasks with no modification intent
[codex] - Work already covered by specialized skills such as `bug-detective`, `architecture-design`, or `tdd-guide`
[codex] - Configuration-only changes
[codex] - Documentation-only writing
[codex] 
[codex] ## Core Checklist
[codex] 
[codex] ### Before Starting
[codex] 
[codex] - [ ] **Read before modify** - Must read target file with Read tool before making changes
[codex] - [ ] **Understand context** - Confirm understanding of existing code logic and design intent
[codex] 
[codex] ### During Coding
[codex] 
[codex] - [ ] **Minimal changes** - Only change what's necessary, no over-engineering, no unrelated features
[codex] - [ ] **Type safety** - Add type hints for Python, avoid `any` in TypeScript
[codex] - [ ] **Security check** - Avoid command injection, XSS, SQL injection vulnerabilities
[codex] 
[codex] ### After Completion
[codex] 
[codex] - [ ] **Verify execution** - Ensure code runs correctly with no syntax errors
[codex] - [ ] **Clean up** - Remove print/console.log debug statements and temporary files
[codex] - [ ] **Brief summary** - Inform user what was changed and the scope of impact
[codex] 
[codex] ## Quick Reference
[codex] 
[codex] ### Common Mistakes to Avoid
[codex] 
[codex] ```python
[codex] # ❌ Don't
[codex] def process(data=[]):  # Mutable default argument
[codex]     pass
[codex] 
[codex] # ✅ Should
[codex] def process(data: list | None = None):
[codex]     data = data or []
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] ```python
[codex] # ❌ Don't
[codex] except:  # Bare except
[codex]     pass
[codex] 
[codex] # ✅ Should
[codex] except ValueError as e:
[codex]     logger.error(f"Processing failed: {e}")
[codex]     raise
[codex] ```
[codex] 
[codex] ### Security Check Points
[codex] 
[codex] - User input must be validated/escaped
[codex] - Use pathlib for file paths, avoid path traversal
[codex] - Never hardcode sensitive info (API keys, passwords)
[codex] 
